1. Elia Stellaria is a celestial messenger from beyond the skies who journeyed to Earth to spread comfort through the internet. (Verbatim: "Today, one such tale shall emerge of a celestial messenger from beyond the skies... So she grabbed her bag and journeyed to Earth to use something much better, the internet.")

2. Elia died during her journey to Earth but was reincarnated as a human. (Verbatim: "Elia didn't survive her journey to Earth, but she was reincarnated.")

3. Her celestial powers are fueled by a magic banana, which is central to her identity. (Verbatim: "The one thing to give her her celestial messenger powers, and all messengers were powered by a magic banana.")

4. She is 151 centimeters tall, not including her hair buns. (Verbatim: "my height is 151 centimeters and doesn't include my hair buns")

5. She is half British and half Asian, currently living in England. (Verbatim: "i'm actually half um i'm half so i'm half british half asian okay but i am in england")

6. Her ultimate dream is to make people happy and spread kindness. (Verbatim: "my big big big big big big big one and only dream... is to make people happy okay")

7. She likes chicken burgers, Coca-Cola, sweet snacks, coffee, soft things, plushies, animals (especially dogs), and kindness. (Verbatim: "i like chicken burgers coca-cola sweet snacks and coffee... i also like soft things i like plushies and my dog... i also like animals which includes dog but i don't like moths... i think it's always good to be kind")

8. She dislikes spicy food, mushrooms, pickles, bristles (which give her goosebumps), scary things including horror games, being pushed on swings, and moths. (Verbatim: "i don't like spicy food... i don't like mushrooms and i don't like pickles... bristles make my give me like goosebumps... i don't do well with scary things... i don't like getting pushed on a swing... moths can go in far far far far far away")

9. She has a strong emotional aversion to not saying goodbye, influenced by her experience watching *Fruits Basket*. (Verbatim: "not saying goodbye is a really really important thing to me... if i wasn't being allowed to say goodbye i know i would do everything i can i'd beg and beg and beg")

10. Her full design includes wings, white hair in two long braids, purple eyes, hair buns, and thigh-high socks, with a banana as her power source. (Verbatim: "when i get my true form i will have a banana... basically human but with wings i have hair buns and my hair should be in two super long braids... purple eyes white hair and thigh high socks") [end of text]



1. She has a fictional origin story where she fell from another world, died, and was reincarnated on Earth as a baby. (Verbatim: "when i came to earth i fell and i got reincarnated basically i'm not the best with my wings um so so so i tripped and and died but but it's okay i got reincarnated and became baby")

2. She grew up in England and went through school there, which she describes as a tough time helped by anime and games. (Verbatim: "grew up in england i got through school tough times thanks to anime and games")

3. She experienced a brief "normie phase" of about two years where she engaged with society and went outside before returning to being a shut-in. (Verbatim: "i had a glow up normie phase for about two years yeah and that's when i learned about going outside and society and then i was like now i don't like this so then i went back to being a shut-in")

4. She holds both a bachelor's and a master's degree, which are animal-related and included focus on AI and convolutional neural networks. (Verbatim: "i did a bachelor's and master's degree" and "my master's was orientated around ai's and using convolutional neural networks")

5. She spent about three months in the jungle doing scientific work, during which she got lost and was chased, describing it as a highly stressful but formative experience. (Verbatim: "during my degree i went to the jungle... was doing some scientist stuff there for about three months")

6. She worked as a zookeeper at a conservation-oriented zoo, caring for animals like rhinos, giraffes, birds, and monkeys, and notes that 80% of the job was cleaning up poop. (Verbatim: "i was a zookeeper... eighty percent of the job is picking up poop it really is")

7. She has worked in various tech jobs including IT support, software testing, development, and as a SQL database architect. (Verbatim: "i've worked first second third line support i've been a developer a software tester and i was a sequel database architect for a bit")

8. She is trained as a data scientist, dislikes math despite her training, and is proficient in Python, C#, and R programming languages. (Verbatim: "i'm also fully trained as a data scientist even though i hate math yeah and i also know in terms of languages python c sharp and r")

9. Her favorite video game series is The Legend of Zelda, with Ocarina of Time being her favorite entry, and she is excited for Tears of the Kingdom. (Verbatim: "i'd say my favorite is ocarina of time... i heckin love the legend of zelda series is my favorite of all time")

10. She wants to improve at horror games despite finding them scary, and plans to play Little Nightmares as a step toward building courage. (Verbatim: "i want to get better at scary games so i need to take little steps like little steps so i want to try and do a horror game like every now and then to build up my courage") [end of text]



